  "term": "obstructive hydrocephalus",
  "definition": "Obstructive hydrocephalus is a build-up of cerebrospinal fluid in the brain’s ventricles caused by a blockage somewhere in the ventricular system. The blockage stops the fluid from flowing normally into the subarachnoid space.",
